cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "Space-glide quantum walk: code for 'Möbius twists in discrete-time quantum walks'"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-18"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24336241
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24336241
    description: "Version 1.0.0 (the code behind the paper's results)"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.24336240
    description: "All versions (resolves to the latest)"
abstract: >-
  Scripts that reproduce every figure and numerical result of the paper
  "Möbius twists in discrete-time quantum walks: inert boundary conditions
  and gap-resolved glide invariants" by S. M. Yousuf Iqbal Tomal and
  Abdullah Al Shafin. They implement the chiral split-step walk with a
  Möbius (anti-periodic) closure and the space-glide walk with its
  gap-resolved Z2 invariants, and run the labelled checks listed in the
  paper's appendix.
